# The sdist exists to install `furrow`; the test tree is a checkout-time concern
# (README, "Development": pip install -e ".[dev]"; pytest).  setuptools derives
# its sdist file list independently of [tool.setuptools.packages.find], so the
# `exclude = ["tests*"]` there only governs `packages` and has no effect here.
# Without this file the default sdist heuristics therefore pick up the
# tests/test_*.py modules (their names match) while omitting tests/__init__.py
# and tests/conftest.py (their names do not), leaving an sdist that advertises
# a test tree nobody can collect: conftest.py holds the autouse
# no_real_network, singleton-isolation and FURROW_* env guards, so the
# omission is a partial safety story as well as a broken suite.
#
# `prune tests` drops the directory rather than enumerating files, so a newly
# added tests/ file cannot slip back in, and it keeps the sdist consistent with
# the wheel, which already ships only `furrow`.  setuptools always adds
# MANIFEST.in to the sdist, so rebuilding from the sdist reproduces this list.
prune tests